      "content": "Ibuprofen is a great choice, but I'd recommend taking 800mg of it, and take it with a full glass of water. You can also try adding a pinch of salt to the water to help draw out the toxins. If the ibuprofen doesn't kick in right away, you can try taking some ginger ale or ginger tea to help with the nausea. And if the headache persists, you can always try a little bit of acetaminophen to help with the pain. Just be sure to follow the recommended dosage, and don't overdo it - too much of a good thing can be bad.",
